OL,3,GNEWSAVulnerable kids' records caught up
OL,4,Ain cyber attack
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe family of vulnerable children whose
OL,7,Fpersonal health information was
OL,8,Faccessed during a cyber attack on a
OL,9,Fhealthcare provider say they are angry
OL,10,Fand worried after being informed 18
OL,11,Fmonths after the incident.
OL,13,FRelatives of some children in Wiltshire
OL,14,Fand Bath and North East Somerset
OL,15,F(BANES) received letters warning
OL,16,Fmedical information may have been
OL,17,Fcompromised at HCRG Care Group in
OL,18,FFebruary 2025.
OL,20,FOne woman said her two teenage nieces'
OL,21,Freceived the letter and added: "This is
OL,22,Fappalling and really scary."
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,349,340,200,160,0,100
